                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "First impression: Cheap Mahjong game.\n\nI am using a mouse. This is nice to click on tiles. It would be nice to rotate with if rotation didn't use the mouse to operate a simulated stick controller. Clicking on stuff also sometimes jerks the cube around. Every FPS and 3D RPG, basically every 3D game with adjustable views uses rotation that is proportional to where you move your mouse. This game does not, it is weird, it is bad, and I refuse to get used to it.\n\nI played the first and the last game of the first set of games. They were easy.\n\nYou're not going to want to play it with this control scheme. Trust me.",
